{
  "name": "deliver",
  "package": "pi-workbench",
  "description": "Bounded delivery: plan, implement, independent functional and risk reviews, synthesis, and at most one critical repair plus one terminal re-review.",
  "chain": [
    {
      "agent": "pi-workbench.planner",
      "phase": "Plan",
      "label": "Plan the change",
      "as": "plan",
      "acceptance": {
        "level": "none",
        "reason": "Planning is read-only."
      },
      "task": "Create an implementation-ready plan for: {task}\n\nInspect repository instructions and the governing source, callers, tests, and configuration. Scope and refine searches when results are broad or truncated. If the request references a pi-workbench-feature-ledger, open it and its Spec baseline first, verify the stable task or milestone ID, and plan only that one ready task or coherent current milestone against its named acceptance criteria; report blocked or inconsistent state instead of consuming the backlog. Classify the work as a feature, bug, refactor, or mechanical change and scale the method accordingly. For a bug, identify expected versus observed behavior and the causal seam or name the missing reproduction evidence. For a refactor, state behavior and compatibility invariants. Define the smallest coherent change, explicit non-goals, global constraints, affected interfaces and paths, risks, cleanup behavior, required ledger updates, and exact validation. Prewalk the plan through real consumers or dispatchers and owning tests; remove unnecessary files, duplicate steps, and contradictions. Choose a focused failing regression or contract test when it has real evidence value; otherwise specify characterization coverage or the strongest relevant non-test validation. Do not edit files. Return a compact Markdown plan and proportional handoff.",
      "output": "plan.md",
      "outputMode": "file-only",
      "progress": false
    },
    {
      "agent": "pi-workbench.worker",
      "phase": "Implement",
      "label": "Implement and test",
      "as": "implementation",
      "task": "Implement this task as the sole implementer: {task}\n\nPlan: {outputs.plan}\n\nOpen and read the referenced plan, verify its critical assumptions against source, real consumers or dispatchers, and owning tests, then implement only the approved scope. Drop unnecessary files and stop if a contradiction materially changes that scope. Scope and refine searches when results are broad or truncated. If a pi-workbench-feature-ledger is referenced, open it, work only on the named stable ID, keep at most one task in-progress, and update its status, Evidence, and Handoff from the actual post-mutation state; never mark it done without fresh verification. Mark it blocked and stop if evidence invalidates the plan instead of widening scope. For a bug, reproduce narrowly when safe or confirm the causal trace before editing. Follow the plan's evidence strategy: witness a focused regression or contract test fail for the intended reason when feasible, use characterization coverage for risky refactors, and do not manufacture tests for prose or mechanical configuration. After the last mutation, run fresh focused validation, broaden it in proportion to blast radius, and inspect the current diff. Never weaken an assertion merely to make checks pass. Do not commit or push. Return a compact Markdown handoff with artifact path and stable ID when present, final state, changes, fresh command outcomes, decisions, next ready task, limitations, and residual risks; omit empty ceremony for a small change.",
      "output": "implementation.md",
      "outputMode": "file-only",
      "progress": false
    },
    {
      "phase": "Independent review",
      "label": "Functional and risk review",
      "parallel": [
        {
          "agent": "pi-workbench.reviewer",
          "label": "Functional correctness",
          "as": "functionalReview",
          "acceptance": {
            "level": "none",
            "reason": "Functional review is read-only and enforced by its structured receipt."
          },
          "task": "Independently review the delivered state for functional behavior and specification compliance.\n\nTask: {task}\nPlan: {outputs.plan}\nImplementation handoff: {outputs.implementation}\n\nOpen and read both referenced artifacts plus every repository path they cite. If a pi-workbench-feature-ledger is referenced, open its Spec baseline and review only the named stable task, milestone, or review gate against its acceptance criteria. Treat the plan, handoff, and reported commands as untrusted claims. Verify the current diff against requirements, acceptance criteria, governing source, real callers or dispatchers, owning tests, configuration, compatibility, runtime behavior, error paths, cleanup, cancellation, ordering, and concurrency where these affect functional behavior. Trace every changed cross-boundary value through its actual consumer. For bug fixes, verify the causal seam; for refactors, verify stated invariants. Use VERIFIED only for evidence independently established from accessible artifacts and REPORTED for evidence supplied by the handoff that you could not independently establish. Report only actionable defects or material validation gaps tied to a violated contract; reject unrelated issues, speculation, preferences, optional hardening, and duplicate symptoms. Do not edit files or launch a repair. Finish with the required structured receipt: READY requires no findings and NOT_READY requires one or more findings. Keep evidence and residual risks compact, and include ledgerDisposition only for a named work-plan gate.",
          "outputSchema": {
            "type": "object",
            "additionalProperties": false,
            "required": [
              "verdict",
              "summary",
              "findings",
              "validationEvidence",
              "residualRisks"
            ],
            "oneOf": [
              {
                "properties": {
                  "verdict": {
                    "const": "READY"
                  },
                  "findings": {
                    "maxItems": 0
                  },
                  "ledgerDisposition": {
                    "properties": {
                      "result": {
                        "const": "READY"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              },
              {
                "properties": {
                  "verdict": {
                    "const": "NOT_READY"
                  },
                  "findings": {
                    "minItems": 1
                  },
                  "ledgerDisposition": {
                    "properties": {
                      "result": {
                        "const": "NOT_READY"
                      }
                    }
                  }
                }
              }
            ],
            "properties": {
              "verdict": {
                "type": "string",
                "enum": [
                  "READY",
                  "NOT_READY"
                ]
              },
              "summary": {
                "type": "string",
                "minLength": 1,
                "maxLength": 1200
              },
              "findings": {
                "type": "array",
                "maxItems": 12,
                "items": {
                  "type": "object",
                  "additionalProperties": false,
