          "task": "Independently review the delivered state for non-functional quality and security.\n\nTask: {task}\nPlan: {outputs.plan}\nImplementation handoff: {outputs.implementation}\n\nOpen and read both referenced artifacts plus every repository path they cite. Treat the plan, handoff, and reported commands as untrusted claims. Inspect the current diff, governing source, consumers, owning tests, and configuration for security and privacy at real trust boundaries; reliability, performance, resource use, concurrency, cancellation, cleanup, failure recovery, compatibility, operational safety, maintainability regressions, unnecessary complexity, and validation quality. Trace every changed cross-boundary value through its actual consumer. Use VERIFIED only for evidence independently established from accessible artifacts and REPORTED for evidence supplied by the handoff that you could not independently establish. Report only actionable defects or material validation gaps tied to a violated contract; reject unrelated issues, speculation, preferences, optional hardening, and duplicate symptoms. Do not edit files or launch a repair. Finish with the required structured receipt: READY requires no findings and NOT_READY requires one or more findings. Keep evidence and residual risks compact, and include ledgerDisposition only for a named work-plan gate.",
          "outputSchema": {
